/*
 * TemplateExplicitOfLiteralSolving handles explicit template inference when the
 * user provides a literal expression as a template argument and the compiler
 * must match it against an expected type. This includes:
 *
 *   - VarExpr referring to a template parameter,
 *   - literal values that must be validated against the expected type,
 *   - fallback to generic explicit solving when no special rule applies.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::validator::template_::solve::explicit::ofvar::literal
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/validator/template_/solve/explicit/ofvar/literal.yr
 * @Author(s):
